FINAL NOTE SENTENCES
==============================================================================
1. After removing 7 duplicate rows, we analysed satisfaction only for the respondents with a valid 1-5 score, treating the 9 blank answers and the 1 out-of-range score as missing instead of imputing them, because nothing in the data tells us what those 10 people would have answered.
2. Satisfaction results therefore rest on 50 of 60 respondents (83%) and assume the missing answers are random, which is doubtful because Business lost 36% of its respondents and Health Sciences none, so the true mean could be anywhere from 3.0 to 3.7 rather than the reported 3.4.

